  "bodyTypst": "#image(\"/imgs/ap-calc-ab-2014-frq-03-diagram-01.png\", width: 65%)\n\nThe function $f$ is defined on the closed interval \\[-5, 4\\]. The graph of $f$ consists of three line segments and is shown in the figure above. Let $g$ be the function defined by $g(x)= integral_(- 3)^(x) f(t) d t$.\n\n(a) Find $g(3)$.\n\n(b) On what open intervals contained in $- 5 < x < 4$ is the graph of $g$ both increasing and concave down? Give a reason for your answer.\n\n(c) The function $h$ is defined by $h(x)= frac(g(x),5 x)$. Find $h'(3)$.\n\n(d) The function $p$ is defined by $p(x)= f lr((x^(2)- x))$. Find the slope of the line tangent to the graph of $p$ at the point where $x = - 1$.",
